# Jest and requirements

Jest is the runner. A test proves an acceptance criterion. It does not invent one.

- Put the requirement id in the test name: `REQ-003 shows a still frame when reduced motion is set`.
- Test storefront behavior and mappers. Do not call live Shopify, and do not assert on hosted checkout internals.
- If a criterion cannot be tested, say so in the requirement under Tests. Do not skip silently.
- A failing test means the code or the requirement is wrong. Do not delete the test to go green. Ask before weakening a criterion.

```ts
// Good
it("REQ-003 does not replay the intro in the same session", () => {
  // ...
});
```
